      "lineNbr": 8,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-18T14:42:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What\u0027s the code size impact of enabling POSIX support?\n\nIt looks like the `platform_xxx()` functions are already providing a wrapper for the Kernel services.  Can you just call the Zephyr kernel services directly instead of passing through a 2nd translation layer?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 8,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 8,
        "endChar": 19
      },
      "revId": "cebedd2fb4f1dfaa74faf35e4c34088beeaca344",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d8ccec9e_7ba2391b",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/ucsi/platform_zephyr.c",
