      },
      "lineNbr": 21,
      "author": {
        "id": 1149894
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-17T00:26:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why are these memory allocation function needed? Why not just use them directly? https://docs.zephyrproject.org/apidoc/latest/string_8h.html#af0f01bffcd16daa9143f6014d10a25ad",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 21,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 21,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "cebedd2fb4f1dfaa74faf35e4c34088beeaca344",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "77a0c3c4_02978e8b",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/ucsi/platform_zephyr.c",
        "patchSetId": 28
      },
      "lineNbr": 21,
      "author": {
        "id": 1365249
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-17T20:44:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`um_ppm` (where this code originally comes from) was written to be easily portable to other platforms (Zephyr, kernel, other OS-es) and defines the platform header for memory operations, task operations, locking and signaling. I think Keith gave feedback early on to do static allocations instead of dynamic hence the implementations are zero-ed out here.\n\nYou can see how these apis are used in https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/extra/um_ppm/. I think refactoring this implementation to remove dynamic allocations entirely from common code is a fair request but we\u0027d probably do this as a follow-up.",
      "parentUuid": "d8ccec9e_7ba2391b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 21,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 21,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "cebedd2fb4f1dfaa74faf35e4c34088beeaca344",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
